{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "54", "x": 0.9032117274603759, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03053152114325986, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "higher levels of depression and anxiety. Across numerous studies, I've found", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.826077001571605, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "people who regularly procrastinate report a greater number of health issues, such", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.82620782341266, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "as headaches, flu and colds, and digestive issues. They also experience higher", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.8259587902998681, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "levels of stress and poor sleep quality. They are less likely to practise healthy", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.825924649490251, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "behaviours, such as eating a healthy diet and regularly exercising, and use", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.8261425150170862, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "destructive coping strategies to manage their stress. In one study of over 700", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.26469857438786853, "w": 0.8261038631095019, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "people, I found people prone to procrastination had a 63% greater risk of poor", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2930660423122369, "w": 0.8260553688063522, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "heart health after accounting for other personality traits and demographics.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.32139637352567824, "w": 0.7752221638855235, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "F", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3596646507851557, "w": 0.01859382309708816, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Finding better ways of managing our emotions is one route out of the vicious", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.3596646507851557, "w": 0.7661148722390414, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "cycle of procrastination. An important first step is to manage our environment and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.38799500085929334, "w": 0.8262948670984402, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "how we view the task. There are a number of evidence-based strategies that can", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.41632538865482344, "w": 0.8265404143628028, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "help us fend off distractions that can occupy our minds when we should be", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4446557764503536, "w": 0.8266708261040425, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "focusing on the thing we should be getting on with. For example, reminding", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.47301087175797835, "w": 0.8260114881261237, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "ourselves about why the task is important and valuable can increase positive", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5013412218321159, "w": 0.8260552662813984, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "feelings towards it.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5295232891122934, "w": 0.2000525337863296, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Forgiving ourselves and feeling compassion when we procrastinate can help", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5677915286503784, "w": 0.8267489501188418, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "break the procrastination cycle. We should admit that we feel bad, but not be", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5961219164459085, "w": 0.8261644553572005, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "overly critical of ourselves. We should remind ourselves that we're not the first", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6244523042414386, "w": 0.8260771040965588, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "person to procrastinate, nor the last. Doing this can take the edge off the negative", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6527826543155762, "w": 0.8267584849395456, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "feelings we have about ourselves when we procrastinate. This can all make it", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6811501222399445, "w": 0.826817129213122, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "easier to get back on track.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7094804723140822, "w": 0.28128615606574026, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Questions 14-16", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7858686308748994, "w": 0.1689930603934518, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Reading Passage 2 has six paragraphs, A-F.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8241369081343769, "w": 0.4365304151040582, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Which paragraph contains the following information?", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8622815346692038, "w": 0.5445731593976987, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "NB You may use any letter more than once.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9005498119286812, "w": 0.4419728497518332, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}], "source": "pdf text layer"}